! Publisher

One-click build and publish plugin for TiddlyWiki.

Adds a button to the page control bar. Click to build and publish your TiddlyWiki. Build logs are saved in `$:/custom/build-publish-log`.

! Button States

|! State |! Display |! Description |
| Idle | SVG icon | Ready to publish |
| Loading | ⏳ Publishing... | Build in progress |
| Success | ✅ Success | Build succeeded |
| Failure | ❌ Failed | Build failed |
| Error | ❌ Error | Network/API error |

! Build Logs

Each build log is saved in `$:/custom/build-publish-log`, containing:
* Build time
* Duration
* Status
* Build output
* Deployment output

Keeps the last 10 build records.

! API

Provides `/api/build` POST endpoint with two authentication methods:
1. TiddlyWiki session authentication
2. Basic Auth (via environment variables `TW_USERNAME` and `TW_PASSWORD`)

! Files

* `api.js` - API endpoint, handles build requests and logging
* `button.js` - Page button, displays status and triggers builds

